text:
Jihoon: Kickoff for HydrAqua Labs POC — they want SDK streaming + function-calls that emit structured events to their legacy Kafka-like event bus. Main asks: SSO/SAML, KMS key usage, and an estimate for steady 10k QPS (bursty). Any blockers?
Maya: Thanks. Quick checklist: 1) streaming client sample for reconnects 2) function-call -> JSON schema mapping 3) network peering options for Private. I have a small test harness.
Sam: I can own sample code + runbook. Are they on EU region? also need to confirm if they require dedicated (reserved) capacity for predictability.
Jihoon: EU + US multi-region. Sales asked about pricing for reserved pool vs hosted fallbacks. They want cost ballpark this week.
Devon: For 10k QPS steady with bursts, recommend Dedicated with autoscale + burst tiers. Need exact model size profile to calc GPUs; rough FYI: 4xA10s equivalent baseline for medium LLMs. Also KMS: we support customer-managed keys (bring-your-own) but on Private need HSM/KMS integration.
Maya: For the function-call mapping: HydrAqua expects typed events like {"device_id":"...","reading":float,"meta":{}}. We should provide a serializer example and schema validation hook.
Sam: Draft runbook snippet I’ll drop here. Short example (JS):
```js
const stream = await Redwood.stream({ model: 'redwood-compat-medium' });
stream.on('message', (m) => {
  if (m.type === 'function_call') {
    const payload = JSON.parse(m.payload);
    // map to HydrAqua event schema and push to Kafka gateway
    emitToEventBus(transform(payload));
  }
});
```
Maya: Also add reconnect/backpressure handling — they operate intermittent cellular gateways. Add small token-budget tip: enable prefix caching to save cost for repeated prompts.
Jihoon: Compliance questions: they flagged SOC2 + encrypted-at-rest for embeddings store. Can we confirm embeddings in Dedicated are encrypted with CMK?
Devon: Yes — embeddings and KV cache are encrypted at rest. On Dedicated we can use customer CMK; on Hosted we use our managed keys but can enable envelope encryption for customer-provided key material for enterprise plans.
presales-bot: Link -> <https://redwood.example.com/docs/presales/kms-and-encryption|Presales: KMS & encryption docs> :link: 
Sam: Action items: 1) I’ll produce a short cost estimate (reserved vs hosted) by EOD tomorrow. 2) Maya will commit a sample adapter that transforms function_call -> HydrAqua schema. 3) Devon will confirm network peering options + KMS playbook. Jihoon will collect customer's model size/profile.
Maya: I’ll include a tiny Go adapter too since their infra team prefers Go. Example snippet to post to event gateway:
```go
// simplified
func emitToEventBus(evt []byte) error {
  req, _ := http.NewRequest("POST", "https://gateway.hydra.local/events", bytes.NewReader(evt))
  req.Header.Set("Content-Type", "application/json")
  // add auth header retrieved from secret store
  _, err := http.DefaultClient.Do(req)
  return err
}
```
Jihoon: Customer also wants a short security questionnaire answered (5 pages) — Can someone take point? I can share the doc.
Devon: I’ll take the security Q (network segmentation + KMS questions). If there are app-level controls ask for a call with their SecOps.
Sam: Noted. I’ll thread PR with the sample code + short integration notes and a pseudo pricing calc. Will @Jihoon when ready.
Jihoon: Perfect. Small blocker: HydrAqua asked whether tool/function-calls can return binary attachments (images from sensors) as base64 inside structured output. Any limits?
Maya: We support structured outputs with base64 fields, but size limits apply per-token. Recommend uploading large binaries to object storage and returning a signed URL in the function_call response. Note it in the runbook.
Devon: Also check egress cost and signed URL expiry.
Jihoon: Thanks team — moving to action. :rocket:
